      "description": "Watch Sheffield United vs Bolton Wanderers highlights and goals from Championship on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 1, 2026. A Championship classic at Bramall Lane On September 1, 2026 , Sheffield United and Bolton Wanderers squared off in a highly anticipated Championship fixture. The atmosphere was palpable as both sides looked to make their mark on the league campaign through sheer physical and technical effort. Rapid fire start and a determined fightback The match ignited instantly as Xavier Simons found the net just one minute into the game. The home side doubled their lead only three minutes later when Japhet Tanganga headed home from a Sydie Peck delivery. Despite trailing, the visitors showed significant resolve after the interval. The tide began to turn in the 67th minute when Sam Dalby found the back of the net, set up by Thierry Gale . Barely a minute later, Patrick Bamford leveled the scores at 2-2 following a slick assist from Sam McCallum , sending the game into a tense final stretch. Late drama secures the points With both teams pushing for a winner in the dying embers of the contest, the tactical substitutions became decisive. Kalvin Phillips , introduced to inject creativity, proved instrumental in the final moments. In the 90+3rd minute, Phillips delivered a pinpoint pass to Romelle Donovan , who fired home the decisive goal. The whistle blew shortly after, confirming a pulsating victory for the home team in a match defined by its incredible momentum shifts."
